# ─── Local-only paper / demo-recording material ──────────────────────────────
# Paper drafts, superseded archives, paper LaTeX tooling output and
# presentation-recording artefacts. Kept on the owner's machine, never
# published. See paper-work/README.md for what lives there and why.
paper-work/

# ─── Not committed: raw console logs and bulky regenerable data ─────────────
# The principle: committed = the evidence a reader needs to judge the software
# and to recompute every published number without re-billing an API — every
# experiment report, results.jsonl, the cohort selections, the scripts and
# their tests, and the per-run model outputs and sealed run manifests under
# experiments/sime2026/runs/. Ignored = raw console transcripts (stdout/stderr,
# already summarised by the reports), bulky regenerable CSV, and local
# recording material.
experiments/sime2026/runs/**/stdout.txt
experiments/sime2026/runs/**/stderr.txt
# The generic `input/` and `output/` rules above are meant for the CLI's own
# working directories; the run archive's per-run output/ trees are evidence.
!experiments/sime2026/runs/*/output/
!experiments/sime2026/runs/*/input/
experiments/sime2026/*.csv
experiments/sime2026/*.csv.gz
experiments/sime2026/batch-resume.log
demo/output/
demo/tmp/
demo/probe-results.json
# (.sime-dist/ is already ignored above.)
